iv class="image-link-expand"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset"><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="var(--color-fg-primary)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon-noB79L"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>It&#8217;s October 1, 2026, which means that my bouncing baby <em>Bounces</em> is turning two years old! </p><p><em>Bounces</em> launched two years ago today, and as I reread <a href="https://www.benrothenberg.com/p/welcome-to-bounces">the launch post</a>, I&#8217;m heartened by how this relatively sudden idea I had to start this space has grown into something sturdy and sustainable in a pretty short time.</p><div class="digest-post-embed" data-attrs="{&quot;nodeId&quot;:&quot;591c7b3e-bedc-446f-a402-406c28d0a8b6&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;My name is Ben Rothenberg, and I am super excited to welcome you to Bounces!&quot;,&quot;cta&quot;:null,&quot;showBylines&quot;:true,&quot;showDescription&quot;:true,&quot;showImage&quot;:true,&quot;size&quot;:&quot;md&quot;,&quot;isEditorNode&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Welcome to Bounces!&quot;,&quot;publishedBylines&quot;:[{&quot;id&quot;:7009336,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Ben Rothenberg&quot;,&quot;bio&quot;:&quot;D.C.-based journalist/author who has covered the world of professional tennis for New York Times, Slate, BBC, CNN, and more. Host of No Challenges Remaining podcast. Author of NAOMI OSAKA (2024). benrothenberg1@gmail.com&quot;,&quot;photo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/20584d6c-82be-4471-971b-9650e7e7fa30_574x574.png&quot;,&quot;is_guest&quot;:false,&quot;bestseller_tier&quot;:1000}],&quot;post_date&quot;:&quot;2024-10-01T20:07:01.255Z&quot;,&quot;cover_image&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fce61cb09-86dc-40af-bc70-04de8af10d80_2409x2823.png&quot;,&quot;cover_image_alt&quot;:null,&quot;canonical_url&quot;:&quot;https://www.benrothenberg.com/p/welcome-to-bounces&quot;,&quot;section_name&quot;:null,&quot;video_upload_id&quot;:null,&quot;id&quot;:149311877,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;newsletter&quot;,&quot;reaction_count&quot;:76,&quot;comment_count&quot;:2,&quot;publication_id&quot;:1174649,&quot;publication_name&quot;:&quot;Bounces&quot;,&quot;publication_logo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HeVb!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F59ca8d83-d27c-4e43-9df5-cbc8dcc818c4_256x256.png&quot;,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;youtube_url&quot;:null,&quot;show_links&quot;:null,&quot;feed_url&quot;:null}"></div><p>I&#8217;m also proud of how impactful <em>Bounces</em> has proven to be in its first two years. I&#8217;ve been able to break a ton of varied news stories here already, which has led to <em>Bounces </em>being cited by major outlets like <a href="https://www.cnn.com/2025/09/06/media/us-open-trump-usta-espn-abc-mens-finals">CNN</a>, <em><a href="https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/7457793/2026/07/20/womens-tennis-wta-gene-testing/">The New York Times</a></em>, <em><a href="https://www.lequipe.fr/Tennis/Actualites/Apres-le-cio-la-wta-voudrait-imposer-des-tests-genetiques-pour-toutes-les-joueuses/1705701">L&#8217;&#201;quipe</a></em>, <em><a href="https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2025/aug/20/coco-gauff-coach-split-us-open-matt-daly-gavin-macmillan">The Guardian</a></em>, <em><a href="https://people.com/serena-williams-reportedly-left-venus-williams-behind-after-us-open-loss-12110383">People</a></em>, <em><a href="https://defector.com/wayward-u-s-open-photographer-triggers-daniil-medvedevs-two-part-meltdown">Defector</a></em>, <em><a href="https://www.washingtonpost.com/sports/2025/12/02/serena-williams-comeback/">The Washington Post</a></em>, <em><a href="https://nypost.com/2026/09/04/sports/us-open-party-attended-by-top-players-under-investigation/">The New York Post</a></em>, <em><a href="https://variety.com/2025/tv/news/trump-booed-at-us-open-mens-1236510755/">Variety</a></em>, <em><a href="https://www.sueddeutsche.de/sport/sportpolitik-bericht-wta-fuehrt-geschlechtertests-im-tennis-ein-dpa.urn-newsml-dpa-com-20090101-260719-930-408339">S&#252;ddeutsche Zeitung</a></em>, <em><a href="https://www.gazzetta.it/Tennis/WTA/19-07-2026/wta-test-genetici-per-le-atlete.shtml">La Gazzetta dello Sport</a></em>, <em><a href="https://www.aftonbladet.se/a/zAa7O1">Aftonbladet</a></em>, <em><a href="https://www.sportsbusinessjournal.com/Articles/2026/01/08/naomi-osaka-confirms-move-to-img-tennis-after-evolve-split/?issueId=4KWNKAAMDZF5XNTNUEP7YT7KPM">Sports Business Journal</a></em>, and many more. </p><p class="button-wrapper" data-attrs="{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://www.benrothenberg.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe now&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}" data-component-name="ButtonCreateButton"><a class="button primary" href="https://www.benrothenberg.com/subscribe?"><span>Subscribe now</span></a></p><p>I&#8217;m excited for more to come in a third lap around the circuit, and I want your help in making that orbit the best it can be. </p><p>Many of the big stories I&#8217;ve broken here came because of a tip or lead I received from someone with something to share, who passed it on to me to investigate and corroborate. </p><p>I can&#8217;t and shouldn&#8217;t write about every lead I get, but many of them can prove invaluable. </p><p>I know how many people read <em>Bounces</em> who hold influential inside roles within tennis&#8212;or have a peripheral but still insightful view. If that could be you, I would love to hear more from you about whatever it is you think I should know, particularly about stories that you think are being missed. These can be big topics or small, uplifting or dispiriting, fun or harrowing. </p><p>Thoughout my career, I&#8217;ve established a record of doing difficult investigations and protecting anonymity. As I hope <em>Bounces</em> readers know, I&#8217;m always eager to tackle the hard topics whenever I can.</p><p>So, if you&#8217;d like to get in touch, please do! I can be reached in myriad ways: via WhatsApp, <a href="mailto:benrothenberg1+bounces@gmail.com">email</a>, direct message here, <a href="http://instagram.com/benrothenbergwrites">Instagram</a>, <a href="http://twitter.com/benrothenberg">Twitter</a>, <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/ben-rothenberg-2826a022/">LinkedIn</a>, or <a href="https://signal.me/#eu/Kq7psMBfuk0oa0H_7tPhT3b6o_1D8sBSsXvjVL1vDfSbAyrFduVAeptHp-5utgMO">Signal</a>. I&#8217;m always happy to talk off the record or on background, on Zoom or by phone, or in person if we&#8217;re in the same part of the world. </p><p class="button-wrapper" data-attrs=